  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining the Expansion of the Overseas Health Assessment and Management of U.S.-Bound Refugees, Non-Immigrant Visa Applicants and other Migrant Populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of the overall IOM&#x2019;s work with CDC on sustaining the Expansion of the Overseas Health Assessment and Management of U.S.-Bound Refugees, Non-Immigrant Visa Applicants and other Migrant Populations, focusing on facilitating vaccination of Ukrainian refugees and migrants in the EU and neighbouring countries. As part of this work, IOM aims to address vaccination hesitancy and various barriers that Ukrainian refugees and migrants face when using vaccination services. In coordination with the respective Ministries of Health, European CDC (ECDC), UNICEF and WHO, IOM also intends to develop training and tools for health providers working with Ukrainian refugees, helping them to better understand and address needs of these communities.</narrative>
  </description>
